    "probe_text": "The report matches the source exactly. Here is the complete ordered list of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Before the controller runs (framework / infrastructure)\n\n1. **Idempotency filter** (`IdempotentOwnerCreateFilter`) \u2014 if the POST carries an `Idempotency-Key` header seen before, it **replays the cached prior response body with status 200** and short-circuits; otherwise it lets the request through and (later) caches the body if the create returns 201.\n2. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`; a non-admin caller is rejected before any logic.\n3. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`) \u2014 runs before the method body; violations produce a 400 with per-field errors. Constraints:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters + up to 2 space/'/- groups), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (as above, optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `title`: `@Pattern(^(MR|MRS|MS|DR)$)`\n   - `addressLine1`: `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine2`: `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `address`: `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(^\\d{4}$)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[-+()\\d ]+$)`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `registrationDate`: `@PastOrPresent`\n\n## Inside the controller method (in exact source order)\n\n4. **A \u2014 DTO\u2192entity mapping (`ownerMapper.toOwner`)**, which triggers entity-setter side-effects:\n   - `registrationDate`: null defaults to `LocalDate.now()`, then rolled forward past weekends/2026 holidays (`BusinessDay.rollForward`).\n   - `setTelephone` \u2192 normalizes to **E.164** (assumes +61, strips leading 0, requires 8\u201315 digits); throws `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400** on bad input. (This is an effective validation step.)\n   - `setEmail` \u2192 lower-cased.\n   - `setAddress`/`AddressLine1`/`AddressLine2` \u2192 normalized (trim, collapse spaces, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE).\n5. **B \u2014 `Postcode.isValidForCity`** \u2014 postcode must match the city's region range (NSW/VIC/QLD); mismatch \u2192 **400** (empty body). Unknown region or null postcode passes.\n6. **C \u2014 `DisposableEmail.isBlocked`** \u2014 blocks mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail domains \u2192 **400**.\n7. **D \u2014 `DailyOwnerLimitException.rejectIfAtLimit`** \u2014 if \u2265100 owners registered for today's rolled date \u2192 **429**.\n8. **E \u2014 `BulkSignup.isWarning`** \u2014 if >80 today, sets a flag for the response (no rejection).\n9. **F \u2014 `CityAtCapacityException.rejectIfAtCapacity`** \u2014 if \u226550 owners in that city \u2192 **409**.\n10. **G \u2014 mutation `owner.setCapacityWarning(...)`** \u2014 true when the city is at 40\u201349 (`isApproachingCapacity`).\n11. Reads `sharesHousehold` flag from the DTO.\n12. **H \u2014 `IdentityKey.rejectIfDuplicate`** \u2014 computes SHA-256 identity key (version tag + phone digits + lower email + Soundex(lastName)); a full match against a non-deleted owner throws `DuplicateTelephoneException` \u2192 **409**.\n13. **I \u2014 mutation `owner.setMemberId(MemberId.assign(...))`** \u2014 assigns a (de-duplicated) member/customer code.\n14. **J \u2014 mutation `owner.setNamesakeCount(Namesakes.count(...))`** \u2014 count of existing same-name owners.\n15. **K \u2014 mutation `owner.setHouseholdGold(GoldTier.qualifies(...))`** \u2014 true when household size \u2265 3.\n16. **L \u2014 mutation `PossibleDuplicate.assign(...)`** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` by Soundex + postcode (suppressed when `sharesHousehold` is true).\n17. **M \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 the single **DB insert** into `owners` (Spring Data JPA, its own transaction; no entity lifecycle callbacks).\n18. **N \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`** \u2014 builds the response with purely-computed fields (displayName, initials, apiVersion, fiscalYear, membership points/level, locality, timezone, contact preference, age band, telephone display, segment, self link, risk flag, and nested identity block). No DB/external side-effects.\n19. **O \u2014 mutation `ownerDto.setMembershipLevel(LevelCeiling.cap(...))`** \u2014 caps the returned level at one above the highest household member's level.\n20. **P \u2014 AUDIT log line** \u2014 `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\").info(...)` with id/memberId/registrationDate/membershipLevel.\n21. **Q \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent.emit(...)`** \u2014 despite the name, purely SLF4J logging: one structured `OWNER_CREATED` line to the `AUDIT` logger (with an in-JVM `AtomicLong` sequence) and one welcome line to the `NOTIFY` logger. No real event bus / external call.\n22. Sets `bulkSignupWarning` on the response, sets the `Location` header (`/api/owners/{id}`), returns **201 Created**.\n\n## Notes on ordering and behavior\n- The controller is **not** `@Transactional`; each `findAllOwners()` (called ~6 times) and the `saveOwner` run in their own transactions.\n- Checks D, F, H throw exceptions mapped to 429/409/409 by `ExceptionControllerAdvice`; B and C return 400 directly with an empty body; the telephone check (step A) throws \u2192 400.\n- The three mutation-then-read business checks each re-scan the full owner table.\n- After a 201, the idempotency filter caches the response body keyed by the `Idempotency-Key` header.\n\nI read this without modifying anything."
